@@jars creativecommon creativeworldgen
@@text
@@text Creative Common 1.1.03 with `WorldEditSkipStateIdInitMixin` and `WorldEditBlockStateIdAccessMixin` (TODO server #17,
@@text perf.md 11.2 #1). Group A. Any player with op; WorldEdit 7.2.12 in the scratch `mods/`.
@@text
@@table world
## SQ-WE-01
@group A
@commands Boot; grep latest.log for `WorldEdit`, `Mixin`, `BlockStateIdAccess`, `Capability`
@pass Both mixins apply, no error; the gap between FTB Quests loading and `Done` is about 13 s shorter than perf.md 11.1's 44 s
@fails A mixin did not apply: check the target `Capability$4` (enum body class order changes between WorldEdit versions)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootreject (?i)(Mixin apply failed|InvalidInjectionException).*(WorldEdit|BlockStateIdAccess)
bootreject (?i)worldedit.*(exception|error)
bootexpect Done \(
shell grep -nE "WorldEdit|BlockStateIdAccess" logs/latest.log | head -8 | cut -c1-200; echo; grep -nE "FTB Quests|Done \(" logs/latest.log | head -4 | cut -c1-160
look the gap between the FTB Quests load line and Done is about 13 s shorter than perf.md 11.1's 44 s
## SQ-WE-02
@group A
@client true
@commands `//pos1 0 -60 0`, `//pos2 15 -50 15`, `//set oak_stairs[facing=east,half=top]`, then `//replace oak_stairs[facing=east,half=top] stone`, `//set air`
@pass Every block placed with the given state, replace matches it, no exception in the log
@fails Wrong state placed: the lazy id and vanilla's id differ (`transmogToMinecraft` vs `Block.getId`)
@reviewed 2026-11-20
# r1120lr batch fault: WorldEdit ignores commands from the perfBot session (no reply, nothing placed), so the // half is a client row (a real player); the set / replace / undo path through the API is checked server side by /wetest in SQ-WE-03 ("[wetest] PASS SQ-WE-02 set|replace|undo")
> gamemode creative
> forceload add 0 0 15 15
> /pos1 0,-60,0
> /pos2 15,-50,15
> /set oak_stairs[facing=east,half=top]
do {"wait": 40}
> cdevtest count 0 -60 0 15 -50 15 minecraft:oak_stairs
> cdevtest state 3 -55 3
> /replace oak_stairs[facing=east,half=top] stone
do {"wait": 40}
> cdevtest count 0 -60 0 15 -50 15 minecraft:stone
> /set air
do {"wait": 40}
> cdevtest count 0 -60 0 15 -50 15 minecraft:oak_stairs
expect verb=state pos=3,-55,3 state="minecraft:oak_stairs\[facing=east,half=top
expect verb=count block=minecraft:oak_stairs n=2816\b
expect verb=count block=minecraft:stone n=2816\b
expect verb=count block=minecraft:oak_stairs n=0\b
reject (?i)exception
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
look a `> /pos1` line is typed as `//pos1` by the player (WorldEdit's double-slash commands); the replies name the region and the changed block counts

## SQ-WE-03 | WorldEdit copy / paste / undo / redo through the API (the `//` commands by a player: s3_skip.md)
@group A
@commands Build a mixed region (stairs, walls, a chest with items, a sign); `//copy`, move, `//paste`, `//undo`, `//redo`
@pass Paste and undo restore every state and the chest contents exactly
@fails States lost in `Int2BaseBlockMap`: `getBlockStateById` returned null for an id from `getBlockStateId`
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
> wetest
waitlog \[wetest\] DONE 300
count \[wetest\] FAIL == 0
expect \[wetest\] PASS SQ-WE-03
expect \[wetest\] PASS SQ-WE-02 set
expect \[wetest\] PASS SQ-WE-02 replace
expect \[wetest\] PASS SQ-WE-02 undo
expect \[wetest\] PASS SQ-WE-ids
look the copy-with-chest and sign lines match; undo leaves air, redo restores

## SQ-WE-04 | lazy state ids for many-state blocks (first half; after the restart: SQ-WE-04b in s3_A2.qb)
@group A
@commands `//wand` query tool (`/tool info`) on a few modded blocks with many states (an Immersive Posts truss, a Create Deco block); `/stop`, boot again, repeat SQ-WE-02
@pass Info shows the block and its internal id; after the restart everything still works (`clear()` reset the ids)
@fails Stale ids after a restart in single player: `clear()` did not reset the lazily set ids
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb passed
> wetest
waitlog \[wetest\] DONE 300
count \[wetest\] FAIL == 0
expect \[wetest\] PASS SQ-WE-04: immersiveposts:ironpost_truss
expect \[wetest\] PASS SQ-WE-04: createdeco:andesite_catwalk

@@text
@@text Results 2026-10-27 night: console `//` commands are ignored by WorldEdit on Forge (players only), so SQ-WE-02 to -04 ran through WorldEdit's API (`tools/worldedit_probe/we_probe.js`, `/wetest`, 10/10 PASS before and after a restart): lazy id = vanilla id and reads back for 64 region states and every state of `immersiveposts:ironpost_truss` (3,072), `createdeco:andesite_catwalk`, `quark:oak_vertical_slab`; copy with a chest (items) and a sign matches; undo leaves air, redo restores; replace (52) and set (64) and their undo exact. SQ-WE-01 PASS: no mixin error; WorldEdit frames in the start window about 16 samples (11.2 #1: 13 s). Open: the `//` commands by a real player (optional).
